course: dictionary
lesson: 13611
title: The formal word incursion
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incursion is a long word, but its meaning is simple. An incursion is a sudden attack on a place, or an invasion of it, and it is often short. «The Vikings made a sudden incursion into the village at dawn.» The words sudden and at dawn tell you it was quick and surprising.
explain: Incursion can also mean something coming into a place where it is not wanted or not expected. «Sea water made an incursion into the farmer's field after the storm.» The sea water did not belong in the field, so the word shows it crept in where it should not be.
explain: Read the words around incursion to check its meaning. Ask: is someone or something going into a place they should not? If yes, incursion probably fits. Then swap in a simple word, such as attack or invasion, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Incursion is a noun, and it is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in writing, history books and the news.
fact: An incursion is a sudden attack or invasion of a place, often a short one.
fact: «Incursion» can also mean coming into a place where you are not wanted or not expected, such as sea water into a field.
fact: Useful phrases: an incursion into, border incursion, Viking incursions.
fact: Close words: raid and invasion are similar in meaning, but an incursion is often shorter and less planned than a full invasion.
exercise: «The Vikings made a sudden incursion into the village at dawn.» What is an incursion? | * A sudden attack or invasion, often short | A long, quiet holiday | A tasty sort of bread | A kind of boat used for fishing
exercise: «Sea water made an incursion into the farmer's field after the storm.» What does the sea water do? | Dries up in the sun | Stays safely in the sea | * Comes into a place where it is not wanted | Turns into snow
exercise: Historians often write about Viking ___ into England. Which word fits the gap? | whispers | sandwiches | * incursions | gardens
test: «The soldiers made a border incursion late at night.» What does border incursion suggest? | A school trip to the mountains | A quiet party for the new year | A calm walk along the border | * A sudden crossing into another country's land
test: Which sentence uses incursion correctly? | We played an incursion in the park. | I made an incursion of cake for breakfast. | * Heavy rain made an incursion into the basement. | The dog had an incursion of sleep.
exam: «The sudden incursion of weeds into the vegetable patch ruined the carrots.» What does incursion mean here? | A new kind of spade | Carrots growing very quickly and tall | A planned party for the gardeners | * Weeds coming into a place where they are not wanted
